p.src:
For motion along $x$, the Lorentz transformation in $c=1$ units is $\begin{aligned}
x'&=\gamma_v(x-vt), & y'&=y,\nonumber\\
z'&=z, & t'&=\gamma_v(t-vx),\end{aligned}$ where $\gamma_v=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-v^2}}.$ With the component order $(x,y,z,t)$, this becomes $\begin{pmatrix}x'\\y'\\z'\\t'\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
\gamma_v&0&0&-\gamma_vv\\
0&1&0&0\\
0&0&1&0\\
-\gamma_vv&0&0&\gamma_v
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}x\\y\\z\\t\end{pmatrix}.$

